            <div xml:id="d866">

                <pb facs="0903" n="804" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg804"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">654.116/59: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-29T18:00:00-04:00">May 29, 1936—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>46. Despatch 424, May 19, 1936, from Zurich.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d866-f1"/>
                    Please collect at once all pertinent facts and such documentary evidence as is
                    available tending to show that a new and special tax has been imposed upon
                    imports of American lard into Switzerland. Telegraph whether in your opinion
                    this tax is in violation of Article I of trade agreement and on what grounds you
                    base your opinion. Upon receipt of this information the Department will instruct
                    you what representations it desires you to make to the Swiss Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
